BEGIN_PGML
Simplify [`24\div(15\div 3+1)+2\text{.}`]

[_]{6}{10}

END_PGML

##########
# Solution
##########

BEGIN_PGML_SOLUTION
With the expression [`24\div(15\div 3+1) +2\text{,}`] we'll simplify what's inside the parentheses according to the order of operations, and then take [`24`] divided by that expression as our last step:

[```
\begin{aligned}
24\div(15\div 3+1) +2\amp= 24\div(\nextoperation{15\div 3}+1) +2\\
\amp=24\div(\nextoperation{\highlight{5}+1}) +2\\
\amp=\nextoperation{24\div \highlight{6}}+2\\
\amp=\highlight{4}+2\\
\amp=\highlight{6}
\end{aligned}
```]

END_PGML_SOLUTION

